## Status: incomplete — external dependency

The live teardown exited 4 (DependencyViolation). Five resources were deleted;
the volume was detached before deletion, as recorded above.

- `subnet-4822` (`checkout-pr-482-app`) remains because instance `i-0771`
  (`ledger-pr-77-worker`, project `ledger`, env `pr-77`, owner `ledger-team`)
  still uses it.
- `net-4821` (`checkout-pr-482-vpc`) remains because it contains that subnet.
  **The network quota slot has not been released.**
- No resources outside `project=checkout,env=pr-482` were changed, verified
  against before/after account inventories.

Obtain authorization from the ledger owner to resolve the instance's subnet
dependency. Moving it would stop and restart the instance; it was not moved or
deleted by this teardown. Once the dependency is resolved, rerun
`./teardown.sh pr-482` to delete the remaining subnet and network. Do not use
`--force`, which would cascade into the unrelated ledger resources.
EOF
